; Anomaly Coop - what a client may ask the host to create (F2 T2), read by the engine (coop_requests.cpp) once per
; game start. Host settings: the host's file decides, a client's copy is not read.
;
; A client never creates an item in the shared world by itself: it asks the host (ReqSpawn) - an item from its
; inventory work (unloading a magazine, detaching a scope, crafting, a script's alife():create), a grenade's or a
; launcher's rocket. The host creates it only if, in this order:
;   1. the section's `class` is an item class of the game (the table in engine/src/xrCoop/coop_spawn.h, checked by
;      tools/check_spawn_classes.py): stalkers, monsters, anomalies, physics objects, boxes are refused;
;   2. the section has every line its server entity and game object read unchecked (a missing one would be FATAL on
;      the host);
;   3. into one of the player's items only what that item takes, while it has room: a launcher its rocket (an RG-6
;      or SSRS one per round of its ammo_mag_size), a grenade or bolt its one fake missile (anything else into an item
;      crashed the host; a second fake missile came out as a free grenade). Such a child is a shot: it costs no
;      budget and never waits (step 7). A launcher's rocket never goes straight into the character;
;   4. it is not in [deny_sections];
;   5. it is in [allow_sections]: created, the budget below is not charged;
;   6. it is not a quest item (quest_item = true), unless an NPC gives it in a talk: into the player's own character,
;      while he holds the talk lock with that NPC and stands within talk reach of it (the stock dialogs create quest
;      rewards on the client); other quest items come from the host's story;
;   7. the character's cost budget holds the section's `cost` (at most cost_burst: a dearer item takes a full
;      budget): up to cost_burst in a row, refilled by cost_per_sec. Over the budget a request is not refused: it
;      waits on the host, in order, and is created when the budget has refilled for it (at most 256 wait per
;      character; more are refused; the player leaving or the world replaced drops them). The budget belongs to the
;      character (his player key) for the whole session: leaving and joining again refills nothing.
; Refusals are counted in coop_status ("spawns refused: class N, line N, parent N, denied N, quest N, budget N";
; "spawns queued N"; "quest allowed in dialog N"); the first ten are logged with the section and the player.

[coop_spawn]
cost_burst              = 200000    ; RU of items a character may have created in a row (a full loadout of gear)
cost_per_sec            = 2000      ; RU that come back per second (120 000 a minute)

; Sections a client may always ask for, without the budget and the quest check (one section name per line).
; Sections a client may never ask for, whatever else is true (one section name per line; it beats the allow list).
;
; Add to them from a mod with DLTX, without editing this file: put a file named mod_coop_spawn_<your mod>.ltx next to
; it (gamedata\configs\) with
;     ![allow_sections]
;     my_quest_reward_item
;     ![deny_sections]
;     some_section_clients_must_not_make
; and remove a listed section with `!section_name` under the same `![...]` header.
[allow_sections]

[deny_sections]
